      "body": "## Summary\r\nFix memory profiling overestimation issue.\r\n\r\nWhen `max_model_len` is set small by user, SchedulerConfig uses the default 'max_num_batched_tokens'. This creates oversized dummy batch during memory profiling, leading to much higher peak activation memory estimation than real runtime.\r\nIn encoder-decoder ASR scenarios (Qwen3-ASR in our test), the profiling calculation reports insufficient KV cache memory, and the engine fails to start, even though the real runtime memory requirement is much lower.\r\n\r\nThis PR:\r\n1. In `SchedulerConfig.__post_init__`, when `max_num_batched_tokens` is not specified, auto set `max_num_batched_tokens = max_model_len`.\r\n2. Add validation to prevent manually set `max_num_batched_tokens` from exceeding manually set upper bound 'max_model_len`.\r\n3. Normal operation is supported under limited VRAM and a smaller max_model_len.\r\n4. Works for multi-model scenarios.\r\n\r\n## Reproduction & Verification\r\n### Test code\r\n```\r\n```python\r\ndef main() -> None:\r\n    asr = Qwen3ASRModel.LLM(\r\n        model=ASR_MODEL_PATH,\r\n        gpu_memory_utilization=0.05,\r\n        dtype=torch.bfloat16,\r\n        max_inference_batch_size=2,\r\n        max_model_len = 256,\r\n        max_new_tokens=256,\r\n        skip_mm_profiling=True,\r\n        enforce_eager=True,\r\n        enable_chunked_prefill=True,\r\n        #encoder_cache_budget=0,\r\n        enable_prefix_caching=False,\r\n        limit_mm_per_prompt={\"audio\": {\"count\":1, \"length\":2048}}\r\n    )\r\n```\r\n\r\n- **Before fix**: Memory profiling overestimates activation memory, reports insufficient available KC cache memory and fails to start engine.\r\n<img width=\"1470\" height=\"384\" alt=\"before\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0acabd8a-1f8b-42fb-a56a-c94d1f8441a6\" />\r\n\r\n- **After fix**: Memory profiling calculation matches the real runtime requirement, engine runs normally.\r\n<img width=\"1469\" height=\"366\" alt=\"after\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/57895517-b903-41af-9793-e8292825e72a\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n- Manual test: Encoder-decoder ASR model. When `max_num_batched_tokens` use the default value, it is automatically bounded by `max_model_len`. Memory profiling dummy batch uses this corrected value, and peak activation memory estimation becomes accurate.\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\r\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [X] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [X] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [X] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [X] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes of bugs or motivation for features.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: haiz20060684; shizheng3601; KylinSoft Corporation\r\nSigned-off-by: mzgong1121 <mzgong1121@gmail.com>",
